<title>USA: Guidant says catheter gets FDA approval.</title>
<headline>Guidant says catheter gets FDA approval.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guidant Corp said Tuesday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has cleared the AtheroCath Bantam coronary atherectomy catheter for marketing in the United States.</p>
<p>The catheter is used by cardiologists to perform directional coronary atherectomy, a non-surgical procedure where artery-clogging plaque is shaved from coronary vessels, Guidant said.  </p>
<p>Limited release of the catheter will begin in 1996, with full market availability expected in the first quarter of 1997, the medical devices manufacturer said.</p>
<p>Guidant shares were up 5/8 to 52-5/8 Tuesday.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
